"To Premier Zhang Viewing Dongting Lake"
By Meng Haoran of the Tang Dynasty

In eighth moon water's even with its banks, it seems;
The sky and water merge in a haze of steam.
Clouds over Lake Yunmeng steam up in the sun;
Waves surge in the air o'er Yueyang City wall.
I've no boat to cross the river, I'm grieved;
In vain I'm ashamed to live in this glorious age.
I watch the angler on the isle with envy deep.
How I wish to have a fish when I see him reap!

